diagram sequence "Adversarial"
participant "Far left" as a
participant "A rather long participant name that wraps" as b
actor "Op" as c
note left of a: A note placed left of the leftmost lifeline to check that the margin grows outward.
a -> c : a message long enough that it wants to wrap across several words and cross a lifeline in the middle
c -> a : short
alt "first condition with a guard which is quite long indeed and wraps at the width" {
  c -> c : a long self message whose text wants to wrap more than once when it has only so much room on the right edge
  loop "(1,5)" {
    a ->> b : tick
    break "stop now" {
      b -> a : bail {
        a --> a : async self
      }
    }
  }
}
[-> a : found message whose label is long enough to demand a generous stub length here
a ->] : lost signal
c ->] : gone far right with a long, long label to the right
b -> new "Worker Thread" as w : spawn
b -> w : run {
  w -> new "Inner" as x <<ephemeral>> : make
  return done
}
destroy x
critical "lock held" {
  neg {
    b -> a : no
  }
}
note over c: Note over only one lifeline which is fairly long too.
ref over c : One lifeline only, with a long reference name
